It is important to distinguish a compound kernel from G-API high-order function, i.e. a C++ function which looks like a kernel but in fact generates a subgraph. The core difference is that a compound kernel is an _implementation detail_ and a kernel implementation may be either compound or not (depending on backend capabilities), while a high-order function is a "macro" in terms of G-API and so cannot act as an interface which then needs to be implemented by a backend. 
