  * Use a copy constructor or assignment operator where there can be an array or expression on the right side (see below). As noted in the introduction, the array assignment is an O(1) operation because it only copies the header and increases the reference counter. The [Mat::clone()](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a03d2a2570d06dcae378f788725789aa4 "Creates a full copy of the array and the underlying data.") method can be used to get a full (deep) copy of the array when you need it.
