Extracts a rectangular submatrix. 
The operators make a new header for the specified sub-array of *this . They are the most generalized forms of [Mat::row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434 "Creates a matrix header for the specified matrix row."), [Mat::col](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a23df02a07ffbfa4aa59c19bc003919fe "Creates a matrix header for the specified matrix column."), [Mat::rowRange](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aa6542193430356ad631a9beabc624107 "Creates a matrix header for the specified row span."), and [Mat::colRange](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#aadc8f9210fe4dec50513746c246fa8d9 "Creates a matrix header for the specified column span.") . For example, `A(Range(0, 10), Range::all()[](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d35/classcv_1_1Range.html#af5a0207f6f98a69077db8e77898abc0f))` is equivalent to `A.rowRange(0, 10)`. Similarly to all of the above, the operators are O(1) operations, that is, no matrix data is copied.  

