##  row()
[Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html) cv::Mat::row  | ( | int | ) |  const  
---|---|---|---|---  
Creates a matrix header for the specified matrix row. 
The method makes a new header for the specified matrix row and returns it. This is an O(1) operation, regardless of the matrix size. The underlying data of the new matrix is shared with the original matrix. Here is the example of one of the classical basic matrix processing operations, axpy, used by LU and many other algorithms: 
inline void matrix_axpy([Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html)& A, int i, int j, double alpha)
{
A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(i) += A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(j)*alpha;
}
Mat row(int y) const
Creates a matrix header for the specified matrix row. 

Note
    In the current implementation, the following code does not work as expected: 
...
A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(i) = A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(j); // will not work
This happens because A.row(i) forms a temporary header that is further assigned to another header. Remember that each of these operations is O(1), that is, no data is copied. Thus, the above assignment is not true if you may have expected the j-th row to be copied to the i-th row. To achieve that, you should either turn this simple assignment into an expression or use the [Mat::copyTo](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a33fd5d125b4c302b0c9aa86980791a77 "Copies the matrix to another one.") method: 
...
// works, but looks a bit obscure.
A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(i) = A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(j) + 0;
// this is a bit longer, but the recommended method.
A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(j).[copyTo](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a33fd5d125b4c302b0c9aa86980791a77)(A.[row](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html#a4b22e1c23af7a7f2eef8fa478cfa7434)(i)); 

Parameters
     y | A 0-based row index.   
---|--- 

Examples
