## Detailed Description  
#  XML/YAML/JSON file storages.
##  Writing to a file storage.
You can store and then restore various OpenCV data structures to/from XML (
Use the following procedure to write something to XML, YAML or JSON:
  1. Create new [FileStorage](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html "XML/YAML/JSON file storage class that encapsulates all the information necessary for writing or readi...") and open it for writing. It can be done with a single call to [FileStorage::FileStorage](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html#a29bcb12ede10d87a0fcbf89a88b092af "The constructors.") constructor that takes a filename, or you can use the default constructor and then call [FileStorage::open](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html#a14c2c18dc2e29999d03d52a0c24bd91c "Opens a file."). Format of the file (XML, YAML or JSON) is determined from the filename extension (".xml", ".yml"/".yaml" and ".json", respectively)
  2. Write all the data you want using the streaming operator `<<`, just like in the case of STL streams.
  3. Close the file using [FileStorage::release](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html#ad23d5415a06fb4bc97bfa034589b376e "Closes the file and releases all the memory buffers."). [FileStorage](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html "XML/YAML/JSON file storage class that encapsulates all the information necessary for writing or readi...") destructor also closes the file.


Here is an example: 
#include "[opencv2/core.hpp](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d0/d9c/core_2include_2opencv2_2core_8hpp.html)"
#include <time.h>
using namespace [cv](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d2/d75/namespacecv.html);
int [main](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/dc/d89/highgui__qt_8cpp.html#a0ddf1224851353fc92bfbff6f499fa97)(int, char** argv)
{
[FileStorage](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html) fs("test.yml", [FileStorage::WRITE](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/da/d56/classcv_1_1FileStorage.html#a973e41cb75ef6230412a567723b7482da747a241cefee7b8af34c3d804c864ad6));
fs << "frameCount" << 5;
time_t rawtime; time(&rawtime);
fs << "calibrationDate" << asctime(localtime(&rawtime));
[Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html) cameraMatrix = ([Mat_<double>](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/df/dfc/classcv_1_1Mat__.html)(3,3) << 1000, 0, 320, 0, 1000, 240, 0, 0, 1);
[Mat](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d3/d63/classcv_1_1Mat.html) distCoeffs = ([Mat_<double>](https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/df/dfc/classcv_1_1Mat__.html)(5,1) << 0.1, 0.01, -0.001, 0, 0);
fs << "cameraMatrix" << cameraMatrix << "distCoeffs" << distCoeffs;
fs << "features" << "[";
for( int i = 0; i < 3; i++ )
{
